From: =?UTF-8?q?=E7=9B=97=E7=89=88=E3=81=AE=E9=9B=AA=E9=A2=A8=E9=85=B1?=
 <50561019+Yukikaze20170315@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 02:45:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] Vulkan FG input: let the SR carrier hook use a wider
 allocation range

In one session the SR carrier hook failed 30 times in a row with MinHook
status 9 (MH_ERROR_MEMORY_ALLOC): no 4 KiB block was free within +-1 GiB of
the SR entry, so NR did not start until the game was restarted.

- MH_CreateHookPrologueExtended (SR carrier only): try the ordinary +-1 GiB
  range first and +-0x7FFF0000 only when that fails, and only for the exact
  five-byte `mov [rsp+8], rbx` prologue, checked again under thread freeze
  at enable. Existing jumps are rejected. Ordinary hooks are unchanged.
- Trampoline and relay jumps: refuse an out-of-range RIP-relative
  displacement instead of truncating it to 32 bits.
- Tests: run.cmd carrier-range (crowded fixture) and minhook-range.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
